= Data repository — Technical =

Repository trustworthiness depends on governance, preservation planning, integrity checks, metadata quality, persistent identification, succession planning, access controls, licensing, versioning, and documented service levels. Repository architecture is therefore a stewardship system rather than only a storage engine.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* data repository ≠ database
* repository deposit ≠ preservation guarantee
* repository access ≠ unrestricted public access necessarily

== References ==
* NIH, guidance for selecting a repository for data resulting from NIH-supported research (NOT-OD-21-016).
